From 3dea186cdd3fa859919ffd5ae4d3996492b2a826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] docs: document the scheduler, the inventory file and uid
 allocations

README lists FORGEMESH_INVENTORY_FILE with the inventory format and
the first-fit rules, and states which Ready=False reason a new service
gets with and without an inventory, so operators do not expect that
setting the file already deploys anything.

CHANGELOG records the scheduler, the device exclusivity table and the
extended scheduling contract under Added, the breaking contract,
schema and DELETE changes under Changed, and the non-idempotent
allocation, empty requirements, leaked allocation on delete and
namespace-blind release under Fixed.

module-mapping lists the scheduler package and the new tests with
recounted totals (28 source files, 23 test files; sqlite.py and
test_sqlite.py were already missing from the lists) and describes the
allocation tables in the storage section. Rerunning the section 3
scans leaves the conclusions unchanged but moves the records.py hit
from line 18 to line 16, which scan 1 and D1 now cite. The backup
guide lists allocation_devices among the tables a backup contains.
